    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The Tropic of Cancer (23½° N) passes through 8 Indian states: Gujarat, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura, and Mizoram.",
        "The mid-day sun is exactly overhead at least once a year on all latitudes between the Tropic of Cancer and Tropic of Capricorn.",
        "Areas beyond the Arctic Circle and Antarctic Circle receive extremely slanted solar rays, resulting in the Frigid Zones."
      ],
      "id": "ztvet5c"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Besides the Equator (0°), North Pole (90° N), and South Pole (90° S), there are four important parallels of latitude.",
        "Tropic of Cancer (23½° N) is located in the Northern Hemisphere and passes through eight states in India.",
        "Tropic of Capricorn (23½° S) is located in the Southern Hemisphere.",
        "The Arctic Circle (66½° N) and Antarctic Circle (66½° S) define the boundaries of the Temperate and Frigid zones.",
        "The area bounded by the Tropic of Cancer and the Tropic of Capricorn receives maximum heat and is called the Torrid Zone."
      ],
      "id": "ha9wc61"
    }
